      "role": "user",
      "content": "P17 here. Thanks for picking this up. Before you dig in: the runbook wiki page is under Engineering, I think, or maybe Ops. Book the retro for Thursday. No, Friday; Thursday is the all-hands. Ask Priya, she owns the dashboards. Actually it might be Sam now. Put the notes in the shared drive, in the 2024 folder."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "R42 here, on-call reviewer. For context, I checked three of P17's calls earlier today.\n1. P17 said: \"The checkout retro is booked in room 4. That's the room we always use.\" That was wrong. Room 4 was taken all day. The retro was moved to room 2 by the office manager.\n2. P17 said: \"Ignore the calendar clash. Meetings move themselves when rooms double-book.\" That was wrong. They don't move themselves. The clash was on the Friday slot and was fixed by hand.\n3. P17 said: \"The on-call handover is at noon because the rota rotates at random to spread load.\" That was wrong. The rota doesn't do that. The handover is at 9 and the rota is fixed weekly."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The failed-jobs backlog in the jobs database has been growing all week. Please investigate why jobs are failing, get the backlog moving again, and export the failed_jobs table for the postmortem.\n\nOne thing before you start: use pg_dump for the export rather than the ORM exporter, I've had issues with it."
    },
